# A typed copy of a loop reads its list through the storage that was read in front of its turns. No program can give such a turn a stale storage: the turn leaves for the closed copy at every operation that could move it.
# THE LIE, testing=StoragesFromInFrontAreTakenOneWordFurther: the emitter takes every storage from in front one word further: each read finds its neighbor's element.
# Under --aot-harden=ignore-told-ranges (testing=TestsEveryPosition) the emitter holds the storage against a fresh read off the list in every turn, or the process stops by name.
# The list is filled by push, so that room lies behind its last element: the lie alone reads a hole there and no memory that is not the list's.
